The '''Field Recorder''' vehicle or pack-mounted environmental recorder, designed for documenting [[Psi Field]]-relevant conditions during deployment. Where the [[Psi Recorder]] captures the wearer-and-equipment state, the Field Recorder captures the ''world the wearer is walking through''. The two together form the [[Psi-Tech]] session record.

== Overview ==

The Field Recorder is a small ruggedized box that captures:

* '''Magnetic field''' — 3-axis fluxgate (or HMC5883L cluster at Mk1).
* '''Electric field / electrostatic''' — quad-probe array for vector estimate.
* '''Broadband RF''' — SDR sweep (HF–UHF), spectrogram + classifier.
* '''Schumann resonance band''' — narrowband 3–60 Hz channel; see [[Schumann Lattice]] for the federated picture.
* '''Atmospheric''' — temperature, pressure, humidity, air-ion count (Mk2).
* '''Geo''' — GPS lat/lon/alt; orientation (IMU).

Sessions are time-aligned with the operator's [[Psi Recorder]] feed for joint analysis in the [[Resonant Pipeline]].

